<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine firm buys 35,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Philippine firm buys 35,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine flour mill bought 25,000 tonnes of U.S. dark northern spring wheat at $4.10 a bushel and 10,000 tonnes of western white wheat at $4.18 a bushel, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The deal was made late on Tuesday,&quot; one trader who participated in the bidding told Reuters.</p>
<p>Traders said the wheat will be delivered to the buyer in October.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
